doctype html
html(lang="en" class="dark")
  head
    meta(charset="UTF-8")
    meta(name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0")
    title= title

    link(rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com")
    link(rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin)
    link(
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    )

    script(src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com")

    script.
      tailwind.config = {
        darkMode: 'class',
      };

    script.
      function toggleDarkMode() {
        const html = document.documentElement;
        html.classList.toggle("dark");
        localStorage.setItem(
          "theme",
          html.classList.contains("dark") ? "dark" : "light"
        );
      }

      if (
        localStorage.getItem("theme") === "dark" ||
        (!("theme" in localStorage) &&
          window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches)
      ) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add("dark");
      } else {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove("dark");
      }

  body(
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 transition-colors duration-300"
    style="font-family: Inter, sans-serif;"
  )
    .max-w-4xl.mx-auto.p-6

      button.fixed.top-4.right-4.p-2.rounded-full.transition-colors(
        class="bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-300 dark:hover:bg-gray-600"
        onclick="toggleDarkMode()"
        aria-label="Toggle Dark Mode"
      ) 🌓

      h1.text-4xl.font-bold.mb-4 Link Shortener JS API
      p.text-lg.mb-8(class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300")
        | A REST API built with JavaScript and Express to shorten your links. It also supports connecting your own domain
        |  to create a personal URL shortener.

      h1.text-3xl.font-bold.mb-6 API Documentation
      p.mb-8(class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300")
        | Welcome to our API documentation. This API can shorten your long URLs. Below you'll find details on available
        |  endpoints, request formats, and example responses.

      h2.text-2xl.font-bold.mb-4 Base URL
      p.mb-4(class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300") All API requests should be made to:
      pre.mb-8.rounded-lg.p-4(class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800")
        code https://link-shortener-js-api.vercel.app/

      h2.text-2xl.font-bold.mb-6 Endpoints

      h3.text-xl.font-bold.mb-4 1. Short a long URL
      p.mb-4(class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300") Pass your long URL to create a short URL.

      ul.list-disc.list-inside.mb-6(class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300")
        li
          strong URL:
          |  /short
        li
          strong Method:
          |  POST
        li
          strong Parameters:
          ul.list-disc.list-inside.ml-6
            li
              code long_url
              |  (string, required): Long URL that you want to shorten.

      h4.text-lg.font-bold.mb-4 Example Request
      pre.mb-6.rounded-lg.p-4(class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800")
        code.
          curl --location 'https://link-shortener-js-api.vercel.app/short' \
          --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
          --data '{"long_url": "https://www.example.com"}'

      h4.text-lg.font-bold.mb-4 Example Response
      pre.mb-8.rounded-lg.p-4(class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800")
        code.
          {
            "shortID": "cdb4d88d",
            "longURL": "https://www.example.com",
            "_id": "66c7855b76e819ccb7098116",
            "__v": 0
          }

      h3.text-xl.font-bold.mb-4 2. Retrieve a longURL
      p.mb-4(class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300") Get the value of the long URL by its shortID.

      ul.list-disc.list-inside.mb-6(class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300")
        li
          strong URL:
          |  /{shortID}
        li
          strong Method:
          |  GET
        li
          strong Parameters:
          ul.list-disc.list-inside.ml-6
            li
              code shortID
              |  (string, optional): The shortID of the longURL.

      h4.text-lg.font-bold.mb-4 Example Request
      pre.mb-6.rounded-lg.p-4(class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800")
        code curl --location 'https://localhost:3000/{shortID}'

      h4.text-lg.font-bold.mb-4 Example Response
      pre.mb-8.rounded-lg.p-4(class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800")
        code https://www.example.com

      h2.text-2xl.font-bold.mb-6 Error Handling
      p.mb-8(class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300")
        | The API uses conventional HTTP response codes to indicate the success or failure of an API request. Codes in the
        |  2xx range indicate success, codes in the 4xx range indicate an error due to invalid input, and codes in the 5xx
        |  range indicate server-side errors.

      h3.text-xl.font-bold.mb-4 Example Error Response
      pre.mb-8.rounded-lg.p-4(class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800")
        code.
          {
            "error": {
              "code": 400,
              "message": "Invalid request: Missing required field 'title'"
            }
          }
